# Simplified Replication

This repository contains the Stata code and final dataset for a simplified country-level replication of the paper "Svaleryd, Helena and Jonas Vlachos. “Financial markets, the pa4ern of industrial specializabon
and comparabve advantage: Evidence from OECD countries.” European Economic Review, 49
(2005): 113-144.

I also did the replication of Wu, Alice. “Gendered Language on the Economics Job Market Rumors Forum.” AEA Papers and
Proceedings 108 (2018): 175-179.
So if the FinMarket one doesn't work, please check out the alternative replication work so that I can guarantee that I have finished the assignment.

## Overview

The original paper examines how financial development affects industry specialization across countries, using industry-level external finance dependence (FININT from Rajan & Zingales, 1998) interacted with country-level financial indicators. Due to data limitations (mismatched industry codes in available OECD files), this replication uses **country-level aggregation** and focuses on the Balassa index as the dependent variable (larger sample than ln(r)).

Key findings:
- FININT × Ln(MCAP) is positive and marginally significant (coefficient 6.870–7.171, p ≈ 0.075–0.080).
- Results partially support the original hypothesis that financial development promotes comparative advantage in financially dependent sectors.

## Files

- `replication_summary.do` — Main Stata script: loads final data, runs regressions, outputs Table 1
- `FINAL_replication_dataset.dta` — Final merged dataset (17 OECD countries) with:
  - Dependent variables: ln_r, balassa
  - Financial indicators: ln_mcap, ln_strade, ln_dc, ln_lly
  - FININT interactions: finint_mcap, finint_strade, finint_dc, finint_lly
  - Controls: ln_secsch, ln_kapw1, ln_agriw, ln_rwoodew, minority, creditor, acstan
- `table1_final.csv` — Regression results table (baseline + extension with controls)
- `final_log.txt` — Log file with full command history and outputs (optional)

