## Key Results Summary

| Variable              | Coefficient | Std. Err. | t-stat | p-value | Notes |
|-----------------------|-------------|-----------|--------|---------|-------|
| FININT × Ln(MCAP)     | 7.171*      | 3.701     | 1.94   | 0.075   | Positive, significant at 10% |
| FININT × Ln(STRADE)   | 0.949       | 1.050     | 0.90   | 0.381   | Positive, not significant |
| FININT × Ln(DC)       | -0.537      | 0.308     | -1.74  | 0.107   | Negative, not significant |
| FININT × Ln(LLY)      | 1.241*      | 0.630     | ~1.97  | ~0.10   | Positive, marginally significant |

* p < 0.10  
Dependent variable: Balassa index (N=14–17). OLS. FININT = 0.3 (average from Rajan & Zingales 1998). Small sample due to data cleaning and aggregation.

## Limitations

- Country-level aggregation (no industry dimension due to data mismatch).
- Small sample size (N=14–17 for Balassa regressions).
- Omitted original industry-intensity interactions (e.g., LabcomUS × Ln(SECSCH)) due to missing industry-level data.

